<%# The order summary beside the cart lines.

    The mockup charges a flat shipping fee and 8% US sales tax. Neither is
    real here: shipping and tax are worked out by a checkout that does not
    exist, and a US tax rate means nothing to an AUD store. So, as on the
    mobile Cart tab, the summary shows the subtotal and calls the total an
    estimate.

    Expected locals:
      subtotalAud    — sum of the priced lines
      priceFormatter — an Intl.NumberFormat, shared with the rest of the page %>
<aside class="cart-summary" aria-labelledby="cart-summary-title">
  <h2 id="cart-summary-title" class="cart-summary__title">Order summary</h2>
  <dl>
    <div class="cart-summary__rows">
      <div class="cart-summary__row">
        <dt>Subtotal</dt>
        <dd class="cart-summary__value"><%= priceFormatter.format(subtotalAud) %></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="cart-summary__row">
        <dt>Shipping</dt>
        <dd class="cart-summary__value">Calculated at checkout</dd>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cart-summary__row cart-summary__row--total">
      <dt>Estimated total</dt>
      <dd><%= priceFormatter.format(subtotalAud) %></dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</aside>
